1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,401
This is NanoGate: a local AI gateway on an HP ZGX Nano.
Every AI request takes the cheapest safe route, with
proof.

2
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:14,479
An admin signs in to the command center. Every number here
is measured on this device.

3
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:15,593
Hover any tile or step for a plain-language explanation.

4
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,233
Let's send real requests through the full pipeline.

5
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:26,488
An IT question is answered by the local model on the GB10.

6
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:30,927
A request containing a secret key is blocked before any
model sees it.

7
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:39,344
HR personal data is detected, and the answer is generated
on this device only.

8
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:44,501
Security questions are grounded in the CISA vulnerability
catalog, and reused once verified.

9
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:43,737
Every decision is sealed into a tamper-evident receipt.

10
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:51,500
Anyone can verify it. Change one field, and the tamper
test catches it.

11
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:56,948
Every request, answered or denied, stays on record.

12
00:00:56,469 --> 00:01:00,997
Company documents make answers specific. This runbook is
indexed on the device.

13
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,993
The NanoGate Assistant answers questions from live data,
on the local models.

14
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,379
It can also prepare tasks, like taking a backup.

15
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,424
Nothing changes until an admin confirms.

16
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:27,163
Every app, employee and auditor gets their own key: shown
once, revocable any time.

17
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,151
Departments carry their own policies and budgets.

18
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:38,379
Alerts reach Slack, Teams, or any webhook.

19
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:46,502
Operations covers HTTPS, backups, retention, erasure
requests and audit exports.

20
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,448
Finance sees measured cost per department, ready for
chargeback.

21
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:58,087
And all of it runs on hardware you own.

22
00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:01,611
Employees get a private assistant that follows their
team's rules.

23
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:09,871
Its answer comes from the company runbook, generated on
this device, with a receipt.

24
00:02:09,819 --> 00:02:14,533
NanoGate. Safer, cheaper, provable AI, on hardware you
own.
